{
    "background_story": "Jeremy was a rugged outdoorsman who spent most of his life working as a carpenter and a mountain guide. Years of physical labor had taken its toll on his hands, leaving them rough and calloused. But Jeremy wore his callosity as a badge of honor, a testament to his hard work and dedication. Despite the rough exterior, he had a gentle soul and a deep love for the natural world. Jeremy's hands, though toughened by years of labor, were also skilled and deft, able to craft beautiful furniture and guide novice climbers up treacherous peaks. His calloused hands told the story of a life lived fully, with every scar and wrinkle a reminder of a challenge overcome and a lesson learned.",
